# Dev Team Orchestrator routing

When the user asks for team/feature work via **dev-team-orchestrator** (requirements, tech design, implementation plan, tests, or a full pipeline):

1. Call the MCP tool `run_development_pipeline` on `user-dev-team-orchestrator`.
2. Do **not** use Cursor `Task` with `software-engineer`, `qa-engineer`, `system-architect`, or `technology-architect` for that work.
3. Those Cursor Task subagents use Cursor models and **never** hit 9router.

## Spec-driven pipeline

The MCP tool runs LangGraph. Pass optional `projectRoot` (default `"."`) — that folder is treated as the **app root** for all writes (resolved under `WORKSPACE_ROOT` or `cwd`). Prefer setting `projectRoot` (e.g. `samples/my-app`) so the MCP package README is not overwritten.

| Stage | Env var | Default | Writes / reads |
|---|---|---|---|
| System Architect (requirements) | `MODEL_SYSTEM_ARCHITECT` | `9RSA-system-architect-free` | `README.md` + `.docs/requirements.md` |
| Technology Architect | `MODEL_TECHNOLOGY_ARCHITECT` | `9RTA-technology-architect-free` | `.docs/technologies.md` + README update |
| System Architect (specs) | `MODEL_SYSTEM_ARCHITECT` | same | `.docs/todo.md` + `.docs/specs/*.spec.md` + README |
| Software Engineer | `MODEL_SOFTWARE_ENGINEER` | `9RSE-software-engineer-free` | Implements **one** pending spec at a time; marks todo |
| QA Engineer | `MODEL_QA_ENGINEER` | `9RQA-qa-free` | Tests per spec; runs tests; SE fix loop on failure |
| Orchestrator finalize | (no LLM) | — | README pipeline status |

**Docs-only:** pass `docsOnly: true` (or CLI `npm run pipeline:docs` / `--docs-only`) to run through todo+specs + finalize (no SE/QA).

**CLI:** `npm run pipeline -- --project-root samples/foo "idea…"` and `--docs-only`.

**Graph viz:** `npm run graph` prints Mermaid and writes `.docs/langgraph.mmd`.

```text
❌ BAD:  Task(subagent_type="qa-engineer")
✅ GOOD: CallDynamicTool(user-dev-team-orchestrator.run_development_pipeline)
```

Exception: editing **this** MCP server's own source (e.g. `src/orchestrator.ts`) may use normal tools; still prefer not to fake team roles via Task when the user expected a 9router pipeline run.
